Upstream bug: JWT auth never authorizes client-supplied fallbacks
(`fallbacks`, `context_window_fallbacks`, ...). common_checks covers only the
primary model; the virtual-key, custom-auth, and Responses WebSocket
first-frame paths call _enforce_key_and_fallback_model_access, but the HTTP
JWT path does not, so a JWT user restricted to one model can name a denied
model as a fallback and be served by it.

Run the same check on the JWT path after the token is built.

Removal check: fallback check in tests/verify_jwt_auth.py
diff --git a/litellm/proxy/auth/user_api_key_auth.py b/litellm/proxy/auth/user_api_key_auth.py
--- a/litellm/proxy/auth/user_api_key_auth.py
+++ b/litellm/proxy/auth/user_api_key_auth.py
@@ -1486,6 +1486,7 @@
